1,Jùjú music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jùjú_music,"Jùjú (Yoruba: [d͡ʒùd͡ʒú]) is a style of Yoruba popular music, originated in Lagos, Nigeria. [1] It first began developing in the 1920s with Tunde King (Abdulrafiu Babatunde King). [2] Early styles of jùjú music consisted of banjo or acoustic guitar, drums, gourd rattle, tambourine, and vocals. [2] Call-and-response singing is common in jùjú music along with harmonies, repetitive ...",Juu,Afro-Asiatic
